## Managed calls under LTO (ImplementationPlan.md 5.20.6 MW3, 5.20.7 MK5,
## 5.20.4 MR2 and MR4, milestone MC-1). lto.ll (for
## x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu-msil and, as lto-net.ll, msil64-unknown-dotnet)
## makes managed calls of a static field, a constructor with a UTF-8
## string, a value-type instance method, an enum over int64, msil_catch and
## an ASSEMBLY argument; llvm-as makes the bitcode inputs.
## - MK5: a bitcode input's undefined '__msil_mc.<symbol>' is never late
##   bound: with libw.so.1, a native stand-in library that exports
##   '__msil_mc.widget_count', the LTO image still links silently, LTO code
##   generation defines the stub, and the image has no .pinvokeimpl and no
##   moduleref. The members bind as in an object link (managed-calls.test).
## - MR2 (reason 2): cname.ll defines the C name 'widget_count'; the stub
##   never merges with it: the image has both methods, and main calls the
##   stub.
## - MW3: --lto-emit-asm writes the stubs with their bodies as 'assembly'
##   methods; scopes are [mscorlib], or the declaration's ASSEMBLY
##   ([ContosoText] for Measure), and never bound, with or without
##   --reference (the same text), and ilasm assembles it. Its stubs also
##   carry whole-program text's run-time checks (point_sum's kind check,
##   set_wide's enum check), which managed-calls-text-checks.test pins.
## - With --reference, msil-ld runs 5.20.7's checks on the merged module in
##   both modes: T-M7 for an int32 passed to an int64-backed enum
##   (wide.ll), in the LTO image and under --lto-emit-asm; without
##   --reference, --lto-emit-asm binds nothing and makes none of them, and the
##   same input writes its text.
## - MR4, T-M17 (5.20.4 MR4 and 5.20.3 T-M17 as amended in section 12: a
##   unit counts when its compiled code still declares the managed call, in
##   every link mode): two units that declare one function with different
##   msil_method arguments (pick1.ll and pick2.ll: Guarded(int32) and
##   Check(bool), the same C type int(int)) or different msil_catch
##   arguments (catch1.ll and catch2.ll: Contoso.WidgetException=5 and =6),
##   and each call it, fail with
##   'managed call '<f>' is declared with different 'msil_method' or 'msil_catch' arguments in different translation units',
##   once, and write no output: as bitcode inputs, which msil-ld compares
##   before LTO, for the image and for --lto-emit-asm, and as CIL objects,
##   whose stubs msil-ld compares, in both input orders (the objects used to
##   link, each with its own stub). managed-calls-units.test has the units
##   whose optimizer deletes the call, ThinLTO and LTO partitions,
##   managed-calls-late.test the archive members that LTO's code extracts,
##   and managed-calls-assembly.test the declarations that differ only in
##   ASSEMBLY.
## - 5.20.4 and MR4 as amended in section 12 (2026-11-04, the row '5.20.4
##   (IR name, MR4) and T-M17 amended', and MC-1's fix of D2): a managed
##   call with internal linkage is '__msil_mc.<symbol>.__uniq.<n>', where
##   clang's <n> hashes the declaration's !msil.managed.calls operands 1-6
##   (TYPE, MEMBER, SIGNATURE, ASSEMBLY, the conversion and catch lists) and
##   its function type (its C types, and the IR type and extension
##   that the C ABI gives its result and each parameter), so equal
##   names mean interchangeable declarations: the 'static' managed
##   calls of two units merge under LTO only when they would make
##   the same stub. msil-ld never recomputes <n>, so the
##   digits here are hand-written. uniq1.ll and uniq2.ll (and uniq1-net.ll
##   and uniq2-net.ll for msil64-unknown-dotnet) declare different members
##   under different names, Contoso.Widget::Guarded(int32) as int(int) and
##   Contoso.Widget::Mix(float32, float64) as double(float, double): they
##   link as an LTO image without a diagnostic and --lto-emit-asm writes
##   two stubs, each calling its own member. uniq3.ll and uniq4.ll declare
##   one name, 'get.__uniq.333', with equal entries
##   (Contoso.Widget::Guarded(int32) as int(int)), and each unit calls it:
##   they link in both unit orders without T-M17, as an LTO image and under
##   --lto-emit-asm with and without --reference, with one stub that both
##   callers call. Two units that give one external managed call different
##   C prototypes (proto1.ll and proto2.ll, msil64-unknown-dotnet: set_mode
##   for an int32-backed enum as void(int) and as void(long long)) fail with
##   T-M17 in both unit orders, as an LTO image, under --lto-emit-asm with
##   and without --reference and as CIL objects, once, and never with T-M10
##   ('taking the address ...') or T-M7: msil-ld decides T-M17 before LTO
##   (the declarations' function types differ), and in an object link from
##   the stubs, before the writer's T-M7. The objects used to get T-M7 for
##   the 64-bit one, and --lto-emit-asm with references once gave T-M7 for
##   the 64-bit unit when proto2.ll came first.
## - -g -O2 (dbg.ll and dbg-net.ll): a managed-call declaration with a
##   DISubprogram that is not distinct (a declaration's, 'declare !dbg'),
##   called from a main with a distinct one, links under --lto-emit-asm and
##   as an LTO image without a diagnostic, and the stub is written.
## - --lto-emit-asm checks the merged module's declarations by its own
##   implementation (checkManagedCallDeclarations, from the attributes), so
##   managed-calls-checks.test's inputs run here as bitcode (l-<name>.ll)
##   and each text is pinned whole under --lto-emit-asm with --reference:
##   T-M9 (l-notexc.ll), T-M16 (l-refval.ll, l-valref.ll; and for the
##   conversions: l-boxedref.ll, l-objval.ll, l-ctorval.ll, l-ctorref.ll),
##   T-M7 on the third CIL parameter (l-third.ll) and for a uint8-backed
##   enum (l-small.ll), T-M7's result form (l-origin-int.ll, l-wide-res.ll,
##   l-wide-field.ll; l-res-ok.ll and l-field-ok.ll link) and T-M18
##   (l-literal.ll). LTO image links of l-third.ll, l-notexc.ll,
##   l-ctorval.ll, l-wide-res.ll and l-literal.ll give the same texts (the
##   object check of the LTO object). T-M8 applies to LTO image links (the
##   object check of the LTO object) and not to --lto-emit-asm: without
##   references, wide.ll's LTO image gets T-M8 for Contoso.WideMode and then
##   the built-in-table line for Contoso.Widget, and l-exc-val.ll
##   (msil64-unknown-dotnet: a table member, Exception::get_HResult(), on
##   'valuetype System.Exception') gets T-M8 alone; --lto-emit-asm checks
##   nothing without references and writes the text of both (MW3).
## - MR2 (reason 4): mr2a.ll declares f with msil_method and defines g,
##   which calls it; mr2b.ll declares a plain 'int f(int)' and main calls f
##   and g. The plain f is never the stub: 'undefined symbol: f', referenced
##   by mr2b.bc's main, for the LTO image and for --lto-emit-asm
##   (managed-calls.test has the objects).
## - The access of a 'this-val' or 'this-gch' instance method (5.20.3 MS5,
##   5.20.5 ML2 (2) and 5.20.7 MK2 as amended in section 12, 2026-11-04, by
##   the row that supersedes the 'constrained. V' + 'callvirt' row): in LTO
##   code generation msil-ld sets 'msil-managed-decl' on each such call it
##   can bind, and the backend writes the final form directly, without the
##   placeholder and without 'nop's. inh.ll (and inh-net.ll for
##   msil64-unknown-dotnet) calls Contoso.Point::Sum(), which Point
##   declares, GetHashCode() and the non-virtual GetType(), which Point
##   inherits from System.ValueType and System.Object (FakeRuntime.il), and
##   GCHandle::Free() through a 'this' GCHandle. --lto-emit-asm with
##   references prints 'call V::M' for Sum and Free and 'constrained. V'
##   then 'callvirt [mscorlib]D::M' for the inherited members (ATEXT, and
##   ilasm assembles it); the LTO image has the same forms (AIMAGE), and
##   only the unbox before them differs: the text unboxes Point by a
##   TypeSpec, 'unbox valuetype V' (whole-program text's run-time kind
##   check, managed-calls-text-checks.test), the image by its TypeRef;
##   GCHandle's unbox is a TypeRef in both. Without references the text
##   binds nothing (ANONE): 'call V::M' for Sum and Free, the members that V
##   declares, and 'constrained. V' then 'callvirt [mscorlib]System.Object::M'
##   for GetHashCode and GetType, System.Object's methods, which a value
##   type reaches through 'constrained. V' whether it overrides them or not
##   (llc's standalone-text rule; 'call V::M' would throw
##   MissingMethodException, as Point declares neither); ilasm assembles it
##   too. gch.ll, whose one member is a table row, links without references
##   as an LTO image with 'call GCHandle::Free()' and no 'nop', as its text
##   prints it (GIMAGE, GTEXT). managed-calls.test has the objects'
##   rewritten placeholders.
## - char and short results (the row 'fix-loop ownership: ...
##   MSILMCTypeUtilities.h -> fix-6' of section 12, 2026-11-04): the
##   --lto-emit-asm check and the LTO image's object check agree with
##   managed-calls-checks.test's object check: an int32-backed enum result
##   read into a short (l-res16.ll) is T-M7's result form with 16 bits in
##   both modes; a uint8-backed enum result read into a signed char
##   (l-res8-ok.ll) and an int16-backed one read into a short
##   (l-res16-ok.ll) link in both modes.
## - MK2 for each parameter on its own (MC-1's fix of D1;
##   managed-calls-checks.test has the objects): l-pairs.ll passes a long
##   long beside a handle for two parameters of one struct,
##   Contoso.Widget::Pair(Point, Point), and of one enum, SetPair(Mode,
##   Mode), in both parameter orders. The LTO image, whose stubs unbox the
##   handle, and --lto-emit-asm with references give T-M7 for the integer's
##   parameter alone, on x86_64-pc-windows-msvc-msil,
##   x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu-msil and msil64-unknown-dotnet (the l-*.ll
##   inputs without a target take win.head, lnx.head or net.head). msil-ld's
##   lines are sorted, as the image and the text may report the declarations
##   in different orders. l-pairs-ok.ll (two handles, and an int for the
##   int32-backed enum beside a handle, in both orders) links in both modes.
## - The widths of the conversions (5.20.5 ML2 (1); MC-1's fix of D3):
##   l-width.ll's IR integer types are not the ones that clang's Sema gives
##   the C types of the conversions: an i5 parameter and an i40 result for
##   the uint8-backed Contoso.SmallMode, an i32 result for System.Math::Max's
##   int64, an i64 parameter for System.Math::Abs's int32 and an i24 for
##   System.GCCollectionMode. The LTO image and --lto-emit-asm, with and
##   without --reference, refuse each declaration with llc's text,
##   'managed call '<f>' has invalid "msil-managed-*" attributes: parameter <i>: conversion '<c>' does not fit the .NET type '<T>' and the IR type '<ty>''
##   (or 'the result: ...'), and with nothing else: no T-M7 or T-M8, and no
##   binding of the members. l-width.ll also has a value type's constructor
##   with an 'enum' result, which clang's Sema never writes (it gives a value
##   type's constructor 'boxed'): w_ctor, an int(void) '.ctor' whose TYPE is
##   the class Contoso.Widget spelled 'valuetype'. Both modes, with and
##   without --reference, refuse it with P0's line alone ('the result: ...'
##   for 'valuetype Contoso.Widget' and 'i32'), and never with T-M16: with
##   references, --lto-emit-asm's checks skip it, as they skip every
##   declaration that P0 refuses, where MK3's T-M16 for the class would
##   otherwise stop code generation before P0. l-widthok.ll, an i1 (a C
##   _Bool) for Contoso.Widget::Octet(uint8) as the parameter and as the
##   result, links in both modes.
## - MK3 for the static members of a value type (managed-calls-checks.test
##   has the objects): the class Contoso.Widget spelled 'valuetype' as the
##   TYPE of a static method (l-vt-static.ll) or a static field
##   (l-vt-field.ll) gets T-M16 in the LTO image and under --lto-emit-asm
##   with references. The table class System.Threading.Interlocked spelled
##   so (l-vt-table.ll) gets T-M8 in the LTO image without references and
##   T-M16 under --lto-emit-asm with them, and --lto-emit-asm without
##   references writes its text. GCHandle::Alloc on a 'valuetype' TYPE
##   (l-gch-static.ll) links as an LTO image without references, with no
##   T-M8. The LTO object names a struct's static members through a TypeSpec
##   parent, which msil-ld maps to the TypeRef (fix-7): the image of
##   l-pt-static.ll (Contoso.Point's Twice(int32) and Total, spelled
##   'valuetype') calls [FakeWidgets]Contoso.Point::'Twice' and loads
##   [FakeWidgets]Contoso.Point::'Total', as the image of l-pt-plain.ll (the
##   same members without 'valuetype', which links with references and gets
##   no new check) does, and --lto-emit-asm prints the TypeRef for both.
## - T-M23 before the IR merge (MC-1's fix of D11; managed-calls-checks.test
##   has the objects): l-t23b.ll defines '__msil_mc.widget_count' (an asm
##   label), which l-t23a.ll declares as a managed call. The LTO image, in
##   both input orders, and --lto-emit-asm, with and without --reference,
##   fail with
##   '<file>: defines '__msil_mc.widget_count', which is reserved for the MSIL toolchain (a managed-call stub)',
##   naming the bitcode file, or the object of l-t23b.ll beside the bitcode
##   of l-t23a.ll. irsymtab lists no local symbol, so a hand-written internal
##   stub (l-t23ok.ll, 'msil-managed-stub') links as an LTO image and under
##   --lto-emit-asm, with the body that P0 gives it. T-M23's forwarder form
##   (definitions of '__msil_mc_ctor.<s>' and '__msil_mc_dtor.<s>') is
##   managed-calls-forwarders.test's, in object, LTO and mixed links.

# REQUIRES: llvm-cil-dump
